  "title": "Dreyer et al. 2023 — A large EEG database with users' profile information for motor imagery brain-computer interface research",
  "description": "A large EEG database from 87 healthy participants recorded during a single-day motor imagery brain-computer interface (BCI) experiment. The data are organized into three datasets (A, B, C) that share one Graz-protocol task, left- versus right-hand motor imagery, with 240 trials per participant (over 20,800 trials in total). It also provides demographic, personality and cognitive-trait information, which supports studies of how user profiles relate to BCI performance and cross-user classification algorithms.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 512 Hz with a g.USBAmp (g.tec) and 27 active electrodes, referenced to the left earlobe, with EOG and EMG auxiliary channels. Each participant completed 6 runs: 2 calibration runs with sham feedback and 4 online training runs with continuous visual feedback. Online processing used participant-specific most discriminant frequency band selection (5-35 Hz), a fifth-order Butterworth filter, CSP spatial filtering and an LDA classifier. Participants also completed questionnaires on demographics, personality (16PF5), cognitive traits, spatial abilities and learning style.",
